# Projection & insurance engines (§19.5, §19.6)

## Parity rule — one engine, many callers

The projection engine's code path drives:
- The Projections page (`/projections`)
- The SOA Wizard `projections` section
- The ROA / EO Wizard `updatedProjections` section
- The AR Wizard `reviewSuper` / `reviewInvestments` snapshots
- The DOCX `projection-report` and SOA/ROA/AR projection placeholders (`computed:` and `chart:`)

There is no second implementation. Do not write a "quick" projection in a feature module. The document renderer calls the same engine.

The same parity rule applies to the insurance needs-analysis engine.

## Declarative JSON-driven, sandboxed

Insurance and projection settings are stored as JSON documents (`insurance-settings/default.json`, projection assumptions). `calculation` expressions are restricted JavaScript evaluated in `isolated-vm` with:

- 50 ms time budget per expression
- 32 MB memory budget per evaluation
- Allow-listed global: `{ Math, currentRow, prevRow, inputs, assumptions, rates }`
- No I/O, no `require`, no top-level side effects

Do not evaluate user-supplied expressions with `eval`, `new Function`, `vm` (Node built-in), or any non-isolated context.

## Versioning is mandatory — old runs must remain reproducible

- Legislated rates are pinned per FY in `packages/projections-engine/src/legislatedRates/<fy>.ts` (e.g. `2025-26.ts`). Bump by adding a new file and updating tenant settings; never edit a past year's file.
- Insurance settings, projection settings, AI prompts, and required-fields configs are versioned. SOA Wizard / ROA / EO Wizard / AR Wizard runs record `assumptionsVersionId`, `legislatedRatesVersion`, and `needsAnalysisVersionId` against the run.
- "Re-run with current settings" creates a new run; never mutates a finalised one.

## Risk-profile scoring map (§19.7)

The 5-question risk-profile maps to a score per the table in §19.7 with bands:

```
5–8   Defensive
9–12  Conservative
13–17 Balanced
18–21 Growth
22–25 Aggressive
```

Defined in `packages/insurance-engine/src/riskProfile/scoringMap-2025-08-01.ts`. Tenant overrides go through admin (§10), not through code.
